1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,333
Opening code you did not write is hard.

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,667
Meet Barnaby.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:14,000
He lives on my desktop, and he reads code
out loud.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,542
He is a pet, so he reacts.

5
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:25,292
Pick him up, and he panics.

6
00:00:25,292 --> 00:00:34,000
Let go, and he falls, bounces, and settles
on the floor.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,094
I ask a question about my project: how
does login work?

8
00:00:43,094 --> 00:00:44,566
Show me.

9
00:00:44,566 --> 00:00:53,396
Barnaby sends the question to Muse Spark,
through the Meta Model API.

10
00:00:53,396 --> 00:00:58,547
Muse Spark reads the project files itself.

11
00:00:58,547 --> 00:01:05,170
Then Barnaby answers out loud, in a
British voice.

12
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:14,000
The answer takes about twenty seconds, so
I have cut the wait.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,976
Then he gives me a tour.

14
00:01:19,976 --> 00:01:35,732
He says where to look, in words, like:
look at lines one to ten of validate dot t
s.

15
00:01:35,732 --> 00:01:43,195
VS Code opens each file and highlights the
lines,

16
00:01:43,195 --> 00:01:49,000
while Barnaby turns his back and points.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,857
If you do not want him touching your
editor, one switch in Settings turns it
off.

18
00:02:00,857 --> 00:02:09,000
He only tells you where to look, and VS
Code stays still.

19
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,318
He also watches coding agents.

20
00:02:14,318 --> 00:02:29,000
When Claude Code finishes a task, he tells
me, so I can look away from the terminal.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,419
Muse Spark, through the Meta Model API, is
the brain.

22
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:39,279
The voice is Phonon, and it runs on my own
computer.

23
00:02:39,279 --> 00:02:45,023
A small extension drives VS Code, and the
pet is a Tauri overlay.

24
00:02:45,023 --> 00:02:49,000
Only the project folder I choose is ever
read.

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,800
Barnaby.

26
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:59,000
The link is below.
